# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for scripts/tsan.sh.
# Guest RAM: the interpreter's plain loads and stores race the guest's own
# atomics and each other, as the guest's plain accesses do on hardware. M7
# loop 6 decides how they become single-copy atomic; until then every report
# with a frame in mem.rs is a guest-RAM access (checked in loop 5: all 36
# reports of a Buildroot boot were on the RAM block).
race:core/src/mem.rs
